<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil pipelines to shut for repair.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil pipelines to shut for repair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crude oil pipelines feeding Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea will shut on Tuesday for scheduled maintenance, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The pipeline will close sometime tomorrow morning for routine repairs,&quot; said a shipping source.</p>
<p>The bigger of the two pipelines, which has a capacity of about 90,000 tonnes per day (tpd), will be shut for about 85 hours.</p>
<p>The smaller 20,000 tpd pipeline will be closed for about 50 hours, the sources said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, the main outlet for Russian Urals crude exports, was operating normally on Monday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
